Limit: the rollback point is not measured against the current build's load-bearing invariants: measuring it that way refuses exactly the databases that most need an approval (measured: a v34 build reads a v24 image as malformed)
Warn: the approval is not bound to a declared owner identity: it lives in a 0700 directory next to owner-identities, so anything able to forge one can forge the other. What bears the load is that the content must be exactly the plan about to run; approvedBy is an attribution record, not an authorization check
